{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And you shall bring out that man to your gates, etc.</b> The translator who renders אֶל שְׁעָרֶיךָ — 'to the gate of your court' — is mistaken, for so we learned in the Mishnah: 'אֶל שְׁעָרֶיךָ' — this is the gate where he served [idolatry]. Or is it only the gate where he was judged? It says שְׁעָרֶיךָ below and שְׁעָרֶיךָ above — just as שְׁעָרֶיךָ said above is the gate where he served, so too שְׁעָרֶיךָ said below is the gate where he served. And its Targum is לְקִרְוָיךְ.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:27.806249990Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}